From 9fd5bbe38853e06f1f450379954ea56b8d823e96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xurong <xuchenfeng@contributor>


Date: Wed, 13 Aug 2025 11:27:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] USERSTORY support more combinations of all kinds of
 partition types and extended DD_VERSION for DD upgrade

1. support more combinations of all kinds of partition types

A partition may optionally be divided into a number of subpartitions. This can be
indicated by using the optional SUBPARTITION BY clause. Subpartitioning is supported
by HASH or KEY. Either of these may be LINEAR. It is not possible to use subpartition
by LIST or RANGE. Moreover, only LIST or RANGE can have subpartitions.

This feature starts to support subpartititon by LIST and RANGE. Moreover, this features
extends to support all kinds of partition type of LIST oR RANGE as well as HASH or KEY
type with any kinds of subpartition types as followings:
1.range - range
2.range - list
3.list - list
4.list - range
5.hash - hash
6.hash - key
7.hash - list
8.hash - range
9.key - key
10.key - hash
11.key - range
12.key - list

This feature supports all of DML and DDL operations as official MySQL. Moreover, it supports
all of partitions pruning for DML operations on subpartitions.
This feature introduces one global system variables name rds_extended_partitions_enabled to
control subpartition behavior. If it turns on, MySQL will enable to support all kinds of
subpartitions. If it's turned off, MySQL will behave as official MySQL. The above subpartition
types are reported with an error.

2. Support extended DD_VERSION for DD upgrade

Extended DD_VERSION. DD_VERSION and TAURUS_EXTENDED_DD_VERSION together
indicates the version of the current data dictionary table definitions.
DD_VERSION is used to modify the data dictionary of the mysql opensource
version. TAURUS_EXTENDED_DD_VERSION is used to modify the data dictionary of
hwer.

Increment the TAURUS_EXTENDED_DD_VERSION version it will automatically update
the data dictionary of mysql.tables table inside existing custormer database.

TAURUS_EXTENDED_DD_VERSION does not support downgrade of data dictionary. If
DD_VERSION is the same but TAURUS_EXTENDED_DD_VERSION is different, the mysql
server can be successfully downgraded, the MySQL server is downgraded to an
older version and the data dictionary is still a higher version. However, the
data of new data dictionary may not be accessible. Therefore, before
downgrading mysql server, evaluate the impact on the database.
